In short:

- Yeditor Core is source-available. You may read, study, audit, build, modify and
  use it, including to write components, for any purpose other than a Competing
  Use as defined in LICENSE-FSL. Each version converts to the MIT license two
  years after it is made available.
- Yeditor Enterprise may only be used under a written commercial license from the
  copyright holder.
- Code inherited from Lem remains under its original MIT license.
- Third-party libraries keep their own licenses; see THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.

